WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.804
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Tuesday, October twentieth.

2
00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:12.391
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.391 --> 00:00:15.282
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:15.282 --> 00:00:16.470
We start in Kenya.

5
00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:24.827
The State Department raised its travel advisory for Kenya from Level two, exercise increased caution, to Level three, reconsider travel.

6
00:00:24.827 --> 00:00:27.596
In France, curfews are in place after violent protests.

7
00:00:27.596 --> 00:00:41.178
The State Department travel account says that after the October seventeenth protests turned violent, media report the Prime Minister's office introduced partial curfews for Monday and Tuesday in several cities, including Lille, and more may follow.

8
00:00:41.178 --> 00:00:48.388
The UK Foreign Office warns of the risk of local curfews and says to check local media to see if you are in an affected area.

9
00:00:48.388 --> 00:00:52.857
Canada updated its France advice for ongoing demonstrations and curfews.

10
00:00:52.857 --> 00:01:01.615
And Australia says protests may continue and authorities may impose public safety measures, with France's national threat level at enhanced vigilance.

11
00:01:01.615 --> 00:01:14.176
On Saudi Arabia, the Critical Threats Project and the Institute for the Study of War, citing a senior US official quoted by the Wall Street Journal, say the Houthis are adapting their tactics to get around Saudi air defenses.

12
00:01:14.176 --> 00:01:21.658
They are firing different munitions at Saudi targets at the same time, and hitting locations without air defense cover.

13
00:01:21.658 --> 00:01:34.589
In Ukraine, the Institute for the Study of War says Russian drone and missile strikes on the night of October eighteenth heavily damaged energy and civilian infrastructure across the country, killing at least four people and wounding at least fifty five.

14
00:01:34.589 --> 00:01:38.635
Daytime strikes are also causing significant civilian casualties.

15
00:01:38.635 --> 00:01:44.572
Ukrainian officials also report continued disruptions to the Starlink and Starshield satellite systems.

16
00:01:44.572 --> 00:01:53.838
On the Pakistan and Afghanistan border, Long War Journal reports clashes between Pakistani forces and the Taliban are continuing despite diplomatic efforts.

17
00:01:53.838 --> 00:02:00.737
Global Decipher reports fresh clashes in the Angoor Adda sector of South Waziristan, across from Paktika province.

18
00:02:00.737 --> 00:02:03.143
A few updates on stories we've covered.

19
00:02:03.143 --> 00:02:12.736
Update on Yemen: the Critical Threats Project says the Houthis are sending reinforcements to Taiz Governorate, likely to try to break government defenses around Taiz City.

20
00:02:12.736 --> 00:02:16.857
Government-aligned forces have largely repelled recent Houthi advances.

21
00:02:16.857 --> 00:02:21.094
Now a few quick notes by region.

22
00:02:21.094 --> 00:02:31.679
In the Middle East and North Africa, Radio Free Europe reports a Revolutionary Guards spokesman repeated Iran's threat to target undersea fiber optic cables in the Strait of Hormuz if war with the United States resumes.

23
00:02:31.679 --> 00:02:35.850
Russian Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov arrived in Tehran for talks.

24
00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:43.388
And the State Department spokesperson marked five years since the detention of local staff of the US Embassy in Sanaa.

25
00:02:43.388 --> 00:02:55.815
In Africa, BBC Africa reports a Kenyan court found cult preacher Paul Mackenzie and twenty nine followers guilty of murder in the Shakahola forest case, involving one hundred ninety one victims, all but one of them children.

26
00:02:55.815 --> 00:03:05.254
The Critical Threats Project reports former Congolese President Joseph Kabila formally joined the M twenty three rebellion as political leader of a rebranded movement.

27
00:03:05.254 --> 00:03:11.744
The International Committee of the Red Cross says an Ethiopian Red Cross ambulance driver was killed in an armed attack.

28
00:03:11.744 --> 00:03:17.777
And the UK Foreign Office updated its Mauritius advice on local demonstrations and community unrest.

29
00:03:17.777 --> 00:03:28.994
In the Americas, the State Department travel account reports continuous heavy fighting between gangs and security forces near Santo, in Croix-des-Bouquets, Haiti, with roads possibly blocked.

30
00:03:28.994 --> 00:03:38.581
In Asia Pacific, the US Geological Survey reported magnitude six point six and six point three earthquakes about two hundred kilometers northwest of Port Olry, Vanuatu.

31
00:03:38.581 --> 00:03:48.269
In Europe, the State Department travel account says flooding across coastal Spain and the Balearic Islands has led to movement restrictions in many towns.

32
00:03:48.269 --> 00:03:55.441
Australia warns protests may increase around Serbia's parliamentary elections on October twenty fifth and could turn violent.

33
00:03:55.441 --> 00:04:04.513
On cyber, The Record reports Ahold Delhaize said a cyberattack forced it to take systems offline across most of its US and European grocery brands.

34
00:04:04.513 --> 00:04:10.325
Researchers say two more Serbian opposition figures were targeted with spyware ahead of the elections.

35
00:04:10.325 --> 00:04:16.363
And a Ukrainian drone strike on a Russian data center reportedly disrupted VK social media services.

36
00:04:16.363 --> 00:04:17.779
That's today's brief.

37
00:04:17.779 --> 00:04:25.874
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

38
00:04:25.874 --> 00:04:34.020
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

39
00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:36.105
This brief is digitally narrated.

40
00:04:36.105 --> 00:04:37.060
Questions?

41
00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:40.563
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

42
00:04:40.563 --> 00:04:42.595
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
